how do you inspire people on social  media so i got a great question from my  newsletter  readers devon love you guys who wrote in  to say  evan i agree with you but i don't have  the answers how would you go about  inspiring others maybe i should start  with linkedin and twitter  what do you think this is a great  question and i'm going to share with you  three tips for how you can inspire  people on social media number one is use  what fits your style  when i first started out doing the  inspirational stuff i started on  facebook i love facebook i was sharing  inspirational quotes and pictures and  i was using photoshop and i you know  those things spoke to me i shared things  that i was excited by that inspired me  and said  this can help other people i'm gonna put  it up on facebook since then i've  gravitated away to spend most of my time  on youtube  i'm still on facebook i use twitter i  use linkedin but my favorite network by  far  is youtube i love being able to answer  questions i love being able to be on  camera  and use my my passion that comes through  to help inspire people  and i think for you and for everybody  watching it's figuring out what  what network fits your style best you  know if you like doing video  get on youtube it makes the most sense  if you're awkward or shy or don't like  being in front of the camera  then it's not going to be great on  youtube right then if you like to write  then maybe twitter is better right you  can write your short  tweets or if you like to write bigger  posts and blog posts maybe you can  have the blog and post those on linkedin  right so it's  it doesn't matter which network you're  going for if you're trying to inspire  others or people on every single  platform  it's really figuring out which one best  fits your style  so you can have the most success number  two is be inspired  if you want to inspire others you have  to be inspired as well  right you have to be excited about what  you're doing what you're sharing  everything that you post has to mean  something to you you know i want  everything i post  to be something that i'm proud of i want  to be able to look back on it and say  wow that's a  i'm really proud that i made that i'm  i'm happy to show that  to my son related to my grandkids to say  look what look what i made right you got  to be that proud of everything that you  put up  so it's not just putting up promotional  crap it's something that  really means something to you that  you're trying to share with the world  if you're not inspired yourself there's  no way you're going to inspire other  people right people  people catch it they catch you sam  walton used to say they catch your  passion like a fever  and so if you're passionate you're  excited they're gonna get passion  excited too  people watch these videos you guys are  you're probably watching this right now  because  you know i'm excited i'm inspired right  now you know i give you some energy to  start your day  where if i was coming on and i was like  you know you need to believe in yourself  it's really important to believe in  yourself because without belief  you don't have anything and you know  that that's my message for today  that sucks right that's not inspired so  it's not going to be  inspiring anybody and with anything  it'll take practice you know if you want  to get good on camera it may take  thousands of takes i've made thousands  of videos so i get better  but you want to make sure that whatever  you're doing is led  with with an inspired intent and you're  proud of everything that you're posting  and number three is be consistent so  many people get this idea i'm gonna go  on social media right i'm gonna launch a  twitter account or a youtube channel and  they go crazy for the first  couple weeks or first couple months and  you're you're posting every day or  multiple times a day  and then it just stops you know becomes  too much work too overwhelming  you can't keep up that crazy schedule  you lose the excitement a little bit  and any momentum that you built up just  stops in its tracks  and you got to realize that for all  these social channels it  it's it's a long game right this is this  is a war this isn't just  a little battle and it takes time for  things to happen  and so you know you may not be seeing  that early momentum you may not be  seeing comments and retweets and shares  but  some people are watching and if you post  good stuff they'll come back  and you might get one comment or one  [ __ ] i remember like the first  you know those videos that i was putting  out go back on my channel some of the  early ones had no comments had no thumbs  ups  and and i remember like if i got one  thumbs up or one comment like wow  somebody's paying attention that gave me  a little fuel to keep going  and so you know i post twice a day on my  youtube channel  there are people who complain that they  can't get one video a month  up on their channel i made it a priority  i'm posting two times every single day  on my channel and that consistency has  led to  growth has led to impacting way more  people and inspiring a much bigger  audience  so you don't have to start twice a day  start once a week but start  and then be consistent every single week  you're posting  if you ramp that up every single day  you're posting  don't take days off don't take weeds off  you can you can pre-schedule this stuff  out too but if you want to inspire  people on social media then you have to  be consistent  so in summary the three ways to inspire  people on social media  number one use what suits your style  number two  be inspired and number three be  consistent  and believe if you guys like this video  you can subscribe to the channel see  more just like it  i'd also love to hear how you're  inspiring people through your social  media channels  leave a comment below to tell me how  you're doing it so that other people can  also learn from it as well  thank you guys so much for watching i'll  see you soon this is a great quest  great great great question it's a great  question  hi i'm thor rafzan from time management  chef dot com  evan carmichael's newsletter epic  subscribe
 

